{"decision": "PASS_CPU_SCOPE", "summary": "The five findings are closed within the requested CPU repair scope at a0f7375; no concrete residual defect found. Actual source/test hashes match the repair commit and evidence manifest. Transitive imports and package initializers are bound, with added pre-existing product dependencies checked against original-checkout bytes. Complete snapshot inventories reject drift, symlinks and special files; receipts lacking inventory are refused. Dispatch retains observed exit status, boundedly drains permitted output, enforces the cap and fails on persistence errors. Reaped children are not signaled; pre-setsid cleanup targets only the owned child. Setup failures close descriptors and reclaim the held child without retry. Final logs support 86 distinct passing CPU tests; the genuine V2 race failure remains preserved. Historical snapshot 0add4b0's receipt is unchanged and lacks inventory. Review used read-only inspection and in-memory AST analysis; tests were not rerun.", "evidence_pins": [{"path": "training_workloads/unified_h1/config.py", "sha256": "991b0de2aac32256ef6186c83bd93b2391f6eccc5b9317796a4238050fa85b5f"}, {"path": "training_workloads/unified_h1/robustness_contract.py", "sha256": "83f9946c92f7928f58234c7ec159fc635eaeced44819150f76185f96427a81f8"}, {"path": "training_workloads/unified_h1/local_dispatch.py", "sha256": "4b11908eeca620962d75975e6cd9739bdda1dfe50c597dbe24edac3e22f06a3d"}, {"path": "tools/prepare_r6_snapshot.py", "sha256": "44ae60fa43e6e45b35f3f6d450f7b721d0aad9a38731a99d1ca73967ae1df584"}, {"path": "tools/test_r6_source_config.py", "sha256": "1147ee5fb697fea5b6474d53c202c8428fe7c6e80ceb4c6d44e2e59eafae5fee"}, {"path": "tools/test_r6_contract.py", "sha256": "778510a53349baebb465a2eabb3df1ff4ec0c75b0c8486b158a40e18db793782"}, {"path": "tools/test_r6_native_output.py", "sha256": "2f12b2a13d72b778e8f66e6b941b908a3d51bd4c0ffbc9e54e0925e03514015c"}, {"path": "tools/test_r6_snapshot.py", "sha256": "08d0945bfac1aeb5518